Creates files & dir's:

Create directories — mkdir
Create nested directories: mkdir -p
The -p option creates missing parent directories automatically.
Create files — touch

View files:

ls	List files
ls -l	Detailed listing
ls -a	Include hidden files
ls -lh	Human-readable file sizes
ls -R	List recursively

Copy files — cp

Move/Rename files — mv

Delete files — rm

Delete an empty directory: rmdir

Delete a directory and everything inside it: rm -r

Forcefully delete: rm -rf

Read file contents:

cat	Display entire file
less	Read long files page by page
head	Display first 10 lines
tail	Display last 10 lines
tail -f	Follow a file as new lines arrive

What does > mean?
>-overwrite
It redirects output into a file, replacing the previous contents.

What does >> mean?
>>-appends
If you want to add more information without deleting the existing contents.

